The point-to-point moves on a serial robot.

pumakins declares its arm kinematics the machine frame as well as the
working transform, since its world is the flange in the base frame with
no tool, so G53.5 moves the flange along a base axis and holds the rest,
from the arm kinematics and from the identity alike, and G13.1, G43.4
and G49 all leave the robot on the arm kinematics.  G53.7 names joints
by number, and G53.4 takes a Cartesian destination.
